{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:94fe7d5c5d6ad54f","name":"T1 Bulk Loader Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-94fe7d5c5d6ad54f","title":"T1 Bulk Loader Droid","revision":19353,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:47:40Z","sha256":"7fd0c60f84ec8bb2daa00fa69d44660126135fd1ee70112763dd9016b96702ab","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19353","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=T1%20Bulk%20Loader%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-94fe7d5c5d6ad54f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The T1 Bulk Loader Droid is an older model Droid still in use through ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Civil War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Civil_War"}," and beyond. Built by Kellenech Technologies for menial tasks and heavy lifting, the T1 Bulk Loader Droid is one of the most durable and reliable Droids on the market. The only major drawback to the T1 Bulk Loader Droid is its size. The Droid has difficulty working in tight spaces, such as aboard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},". T1 Bulk Loader Droids are exceptionally diligent and do not stop performing an assigned task except by the command of their masters or until the Droid stops functioning.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The T1 Bulk Loader Droid is referred to as the LB-Series Droid. However, the LB designation indicates a primary function of this particular subtype of the T1 model (Loader, Bulk), not the model name itself. Kellenech Technologies originally produces several series of T1 Droids, each with different programming and functions; the T1-CW is the \"Construction Worker\" model, and the T1-EX is the \"Emergency Excavation\" model (used in clearing rubble from the scenes of accidents). However, those other T1 Droids see limited production and quickly fade from memory. Eventually, Duwani Mechanical Products obtains the T1-Series trademark, which they rebrand for their first run of Utility Droids.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["T1 Bulk Loader Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["T1 Bulk Loader Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["5th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 17), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 17, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","ref